# YEARLY POINTS RESET: Reset all user points on January 1st at midnight UTC
0 0 1 1 * /app/reset-yearly-points.sh

# Sync driver standings twice weekly: Monday and Thursday at 9:00 AM UTC
# This covers both regular race weekends (Sunday) and sprint weekends (Saturday)
0 9 * * 1,4 /app/sync-driver-standings.sh

# Sync race results every Monday at 3:00 AM UTC
0 3 * * 1 /app/sync-race-results.sh

# SYNC QUALIFYING RESULTS: every 10 minutes Fri-Sun (sprint qualifying Fri, qualifying Sat, with
# Sunday as a safety net before the race). Does nothing once a session's qualifying is stored;
# tries Jolpi and OpenF1, and emails the admin if it is still missing a few hours after the session.
*/10 * * * 5,6,0 /app/sync-qualifying-results.sh

# MISSED-PREDICTION REMINDER: Check every 5 minutes on race days (Sat sprint + Sun main, 01:00-20:00 UTC)
# Fires ~1 hour before lights out for anyone who still hasn't predicted.
# Window starts an hour earlier than the other race-day jobs to catch early sprints (e.g. China ~03:00 UTC).
*/5 1-20 * * 0,6 /app/send-missed-prediction-reminders.sh

# COPY MISSING PREDICTIONS: Check every 2 minutes on race days (Sat sprint + Sun main, 02:00-20:00 UTC)
# Wide window covers early sprints (e.g. China ~03:00 UTC) through late-timezone races.
# Copies last prediction for users who forgot to submit
*/2 2-20 * * 0,6 /app/copy-missing-predictions.sh

# PROVISIONAL RESULTS: Check every 5 minutes on race days (Sat sprint + Sun main, 02:00-22:00 UTC)
# Wide window covers early sprints (e.g. China ~03:00 UTC) through late-timezone races.
# Sends provisional results email ~5 minutes after race ends, calculates points, marks status='provisional'
*/5 2-22 * * 0,6 /app/send-provisional-results.sh

# FINAL RESULTS: Process 24 hours after race (Sun for Sat sprints, Mon for Sun main races, 02:00-22:00 UTC)
# Recalculates points considering disqualifications/penalties; only acts on status='provisional' races
0 2-22 * * 0,1 /app/process-final-results.sh

# Log rotation to prevent log file from growing too large. Tuesday, so a race weekend's
# job output is still readable on Monday (it used to be wiped at Sunday midnight).
0 3 * * 2 echo "" > /var/log/cron.log
